descriptions.job-0gitt3e:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT HUT 8&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Imagine the ultimate destination for those who want to work at the cutting edge of technology, &lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;energy,&lt;/span&gt; and infrastructure. Hut&amp;nbsp;8 is on a mission to build and operate some of the world’s largest data centers for next-generation computing workloads, including AI, Colocation, Cloud, and Bitcoin Mining. We are proud to offer interesting and challenging opportunities for individuals who want to build teams, solve problems, and make an impact from day one. If you’re an ambitious individual looking for a career that is as rewarding as it is challenging, you’ve come to the right place.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table width=&quot;774&quot;&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td width=&quot;582&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Protection &amp;amp; Controls Engineer is responsible for protection schemes, relay settings, and controls design for Hut 8&#39;s high-voltage systems across the program. Reporting to the Principal, HV Engineering, this role supports commissioning, coordination studies, and utility acceptance for the substations and interconnections serving our data center campuses. P&amp;amp;C talent is the scarcest discipline in our build program - this seat carries real authority over how our facilities are protected and how fast they energize.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Some of the key responsibilities you should expect are the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Protection &amp;amp; Controls Design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop and review protection schemes, relay panel arrangements, and control designs for HV substations and interconnection facilities. Produce and review AC/DC schematics, wiring diagrams, and logic diagrams. Specify protective relays (SEL platforms), RTUs, meters, and panel equipment against utility, NERC, IEEE, and ANSI requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relay Settings &amp;amp; Setting Philosophy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop, review, and manage relay settings files and the program&#39;s setting philosophy. Own settings version control and the reconciliation between issued settings, as-left settings, and study models - the discipline that prevents mis-operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Studies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Perform and validate protection coordination, fault, and arc-flash studies (ASPEN/CAPE), coordinating with the Application Engineer on system models, equipment ratings, and interconnection study requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Utility Coordination &amp;amp; Acceptance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support interconnection protection requirements, protection review packages, SCADA/RTU point lists, and witness testing with serving utilities. Drive utility comments to resolution through energization and maintain compliance documentation (including NERC PRC-related records where applicable).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commissioning &amp;amp; Field Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support factory and site acceptance testing, relay functional testing, and end-to-end testing with NETA firms during commissioning. Provide field support during construction and energization - troubleshooting protection and controls issues with contractors, testing firms, and utility personnel in real time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standards &amp;amp; Program Building&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build Hut 8&#39;s P&amp;amp;C standards: templates, panel typicals, settings libraries, and testing requirements. Review vendor drawings for P&amp;amp;C scope across projects and mentor the Project Engineer (HV/MV) on protection fundamentals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT YOU&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;p&gt;-&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; What we&#39;re looking for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;- 5+ years of protection and controls engineering for HV substations, transmission, or utility interconnections (69kV-345kV).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Bachelor&#39;s degree in Electrical Engineering; PE license preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Strong hands-on depth with protective relaying - SEL platforms strongly preferred - including scheme design, settings development, and event analysis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Coordination and fault study fluency in ASPEN or CAPE; comfort defending your settings to a utility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Working knowledge of NERC PRC standards and utility interconnection protection processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Commissioning experience: relay functional testing, end-to-end tests, and working alongside NETA field crews.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- SCADA/RTU and communications-assisted protection familiarity (mirrored bits, fiber schemes) a plus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Rigorous documentation habits - settings control is a discipline, not a chore.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Willing to travel for factory tests, energizations, and utility meetings (typically 20-35%).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE WORK ENVIRONMENT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Full-time in-office role.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT MAKES HUT 8 A GREAT PLACE TO WORK&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hut 8 offers a benefits and wellness program that includes medical, dental, vision, life, and&amp;nbsp;short-term and long-term disability insurance, as well as paid time off.&amp;nbsp;We are proud to invest in building the best team in the industry. At all levels of the organization,&amp;nbsp;we are driven by an entrepreneurial spirit, radical transparency, and relentless growth mentality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Hut 8, you will have the opportunity to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▶ Work with bright, driven peers from a range of educational and professional backgrounds&amp;nbsp;including software development, energy, engineering, entrepreneurship, investment&amp;nbsp;banking, private equity, and management consulting&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▶ Design and pitch new products, services, and other initiatives to a leadership team&amp;nbsp;consisting of serial entrepreneurs and seasoned executives and backed by a board of&amp;nbsp;directors consisting of industry veterans of energy, finance, and government&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▶ Debate ideas and alternatives in a truly meritocratic setting where the learning curve is&amp;nbsp;steep and the lessons come from both senior and junior members of the team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;▶ Build a lifelong network of friends and professional connections at the cutting-edge&amp;nbsp;intersection of technology, energy, and infrastructure&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

descriptions.job-1lj0b9m:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Ripple, we’re building a world where value moves like information does today. It’s big, it’s bold, and we’re already doing it. Through our crypto solutions for financial institutions, businesses, governments and developers, we are improving the global financial system and creating greater economic fairness and opportunity for more people, in more places around the world. And we get to do the best work of our career and grow our skills surrounded by colleagues who have our backs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;If you’re ready to see your impact and unlock incredible career growth opportunities, join us, and build real world value.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE WORK:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re seeking a detail-oriented and business-savvy Deal Desk Manager to support the intersection of our Legal, Revenue Operations, and Sales teams. In this role, you&#39;ll be instrumental in enabling our rapidly expanding global business by ensuring seamless contract processes, maintaining compliance standards, and providing exceptional support to our organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an individual contributor role reporting to Revenue Operations, with close collaboration with Legal Counsel. You&#39;ll work at the heart of our commercial engine, touching every major enterprise deal and helping build scalable processes as we grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contract Lifecycle Management (60%)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft, review, and prepare commercial sales agreements including MSAs, SOWs, amendments, and renewals for vendors and enterprise-level customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage end-to-end contract workflow in CMS, Linksquares and Salesforce experience preferred, ensuring accuracy and timely execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate approvals across Legal, Finance, and Sales leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain contract repository and ensure proper documentation and version control&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track contract metrics and provide regular reporting on contract status, turnaround times, and pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Process Improvement &amp;amp; Implementation (25%)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage contract playbooks that provide clear guidance for sales teams and internal stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and update contract templates to reflect business needs and legal requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify bottlenecks in the contract process and implement solutions to improve efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stakeholder Management &amp;amp; Support (15%)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a central point of contact for Legal, Sales, Customer Success, and Finance teams on contract-related questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide rapid, responsive support to sales requests while maintaining high quality standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver visibility into contract status and timelines for internal stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Educate sales teams on contract terms, approval requirements, and process expectations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate complex legal or business issues to legal counsel as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL BRING:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in contracts management, legal operations, sales operations, or related role supporting commercial contracting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SaaS contract experience with strong familiarity with enterprise software agreements (MSAs, SOWs, SLAs, DPAs, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical proficiency (including AI) with contract lifecycle management systems (Linksquares preferred), Salesforce CRM, and AI automation tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process orientation with demonstrated ability to create documentation, templates, and scalable workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Legal aptitude including understanding of contract terms, commercial concepts, and risk considerations (paralegal background or legal studies a plus, but not required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail with ability to spot issues and inconsistencies in contracts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills with ability to translate complex legal concepts for business stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative mindset and proven ability to work effectively across Legal, Sales, Finance, and Operations teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsiveness and service orientation with a track record of being a trusted, reliable business partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree (preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Highly Valued&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with corporate treasury, financial services, or fintech/digital asset industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with global commercial contracting across multiple jurisdictions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to high-velocity enterprise sales environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or scaling contracting functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in legal operations or as a paralegal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For positions that will be based in IL, the annual salary range for this position is below. Actual salaries may vary based on numerous factors including, among other things, an individual applicant’s experience and qualifications for the position. This range does not include equity or additional compensation, such as bonuses or commissions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;IL Annual Base Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$168,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$200,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO WE ARE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Do Your Best Work&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The opportunity to build in a fast-paced start-up environment with experienced industry leaders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A learning environment where you can dive deep into the latest technologies and make an impact.&amp;nbsp; A professional development budget to support other modes of learning.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Thrive in an environment where no matter what race, ethnicity, gender, origin, or culture they identify with, every employee is a respected, valued, and empowered part of the team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;In-office collaboration for moments that matter is important to our culture, and we give managers and teams the flexibility to decide which 10+ days a month they come in.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Bi-weekly all-company meeting - business updates and ask me anything style discussion with our Leadership Team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We come together for moments that matter which include team offsites, team bonding activities, happy hours and more!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Take Control of Your Finances&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive salary, bonuses, and equity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive benefits that cover physical and mental healthcare, retirement, family forming, and family support&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Employee giving match&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Mobile phone stipend&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Take Care of Yourself&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;R&amp;amp;R days so you can rest and recharge&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Generous wellness reimbursement and weekly onsite &amp;amp; virtual programming&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Generous vacation policy - work with your manager to take time off when you need it&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Industry-leading parental leave policies. Family planning benefits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Catered lunches, fully-stocked kitchens with premium snacks/beverages, and plenty of fun events&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Benefits listed above are for full-time employees.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ripple is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We’re committed to building a diverse and inclusive team. We do not discriminate against qualified employees or applicants because of race, color, religion, gender identity, sex, sexual identity, pregnancy, national origin, ancestry, citizenship, age, marital status, physical disability, mental disability, medical condition, military status, or any other characteristic protected by local law or ordinance.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please find our &lt;a href=&quot;https://ripple.com/legal/eu-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;UK/EU Applicant Privacy Notice &lt;/a&gt;and our &lt;a href=&quot;https://ripple.com/legal/ca-applicant-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;California Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; for reference.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
